MCP execution requires an enabled AgentTool assignment and exact tenant scope.
Tenant-configurable MCP endpoints require HTTPS, reject mixed/private DNS answers,
pin the TCP connection to a validated numeric public IP before any HTTP bytes are
written, re-check the connected peer, and reject cross-origin redirects.

Production DNS must return genuine public addresses. DNS proxy modes that return
198.18.0.0/15 fake IPs are intentionally incompatible; configure real container
DNS or a separately authorized security egress proxy instead of weakening this
contract.
